WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:37.510
I believe that war has brought many benefits to mankind.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.890
The advancement of civilization, the exchange of cultures,

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.020
and discoveries made by scientific technologies.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:49.590
By harnessing the power of nuclear energy we've attained air conditioning for use in midsummer,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:54.420
and late night television programming, have we not?

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.190
Therefore, I continue to tell the story of that day.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:01:59.430
And always will...

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:04.040
My supporters and I were the targets of the terrorist bombing.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:09.540
Suzuki himself said, "If it were to blow up here, glass
would come raining down and create a terrible disaster".

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.420
We must move the bomb elsewhere.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:16.060
Up until mere days before, they had been average students,

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.270
but they supported me and gave their all to the Rising Sun Association.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.350
Those young men, showing no hesitation,

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.850
drove off in the truck containing the bomb...

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.190
The end result was exactly as reported...

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.650
I won't insist that you praise them.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.150
They simply did what needed to be done.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:37.530
However...

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.780
You aren't taking this seriously, are you?

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.210
I tried my best to wear formal clothing...

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.160
It's cute!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.410
Komamori... What an extreme pervert...

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.410
It doesn't please you?

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.770
N-Not really. There's no need for me to be pleased.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.420
Well, I know that, but...

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:59.060
...and that very fact lives on within each and every one of us.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.680
Thank you.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.180
That was actor Shimada Jirou-san,
eldest son of Shimada Hakurou-sensei,

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.310
with a reading from his father's works.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.230
Jirou-san is also appointed as the honorary director of the memorial hall...

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.280
You mustn't be fooled by Shimada Hakurou!

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.780
He's made a shady deal with the allied nations,

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:24.400
and has smuggled the support money allotted for the young men who died.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.400
Yamada-sensei!

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.030
Thank you for taking the trouble to come all the way here!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.900
Where the Hell is Shimada?

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.790
Is he spouting that same nonsense again?!

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.660
We will never forget those three young men,

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.540
and will someday create our own miracle!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.800
So believing, we have prepared the following symbol...

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:43.640
It's so amazing!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:49.770
Souls!

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:00.590
I commissioned this statue from a young friend of my son's,

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:01.780
who is not unlike those three men.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.910
It was finally delivered here late last night.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.910
Uh, excuse me...

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.110
Where's the bathroom?

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.470
Ah, it's over-

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.660
The Defeated Detective, Yuuki Shinjuurou!

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:14.320
It seems you've been challenging JJ Systems.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.670
You show quite a bit of promise.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:22.450
According to the rumours, you're somehow connected to the group of young people who became the first victims of the war.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.180
Is that so? Were you the one who invited me here?

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.820
There's one thing that bothers me though...

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.180
...what is this "Defeated Detective" business about?

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.090
That incident could only be considered a cease-fire at worst-

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.860
I have to go pee!

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.560
Excuse me, I'm about to wet myself.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.140
What are you angry about?

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.170
You're a detective.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.580
You play the role of someone who exposes the truth.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.150
But when it's something related to you, you hide it away instead?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.550
All I seek to expose are filthy lies.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.470
This is quite the fancy place for a nap.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:14.770
I was working until late in the night,

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:15.890
Sir.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:21.210
She was the one who made the statue of the three men and brought it here.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.030
My good friend, Hirato Youko.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.280
This is Detective Yuuki.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.910
Oh, seeing that statue alone made it worth coming here.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:32.460
They wilfully threw their own lives away for the good of others; is that how the story went?

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.630
It most certainly wasn't that selfless.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.870
I expect they shed at least a single tear.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.930
At least that's the feeling I got.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.610
I apologise for the way my father acted earlier.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.720
Honestly, even as his son, I find him to be too high-handed.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.130
The fact that he still thinks we haven't lost the war is one thing,

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.150
but they even say he advocates reinstating the draft.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:52.010
And that he's obsessed with money.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:52.640
Youko!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:56.390
It's merely the opinion of Yamamoto, a Yakuza who used to be his bodyguard.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:59.490
He insists that the details of the story of those three heroes is falsified,

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.360
and that Shimada's hidden the large sum of
support money away in the form of gold bars.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.290
Yamamoto is making this fuss in demand that he return it.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.620
Gold bars? That's pretty deplorable.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.950
He was a member of the House until recently! There's no way he would!

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.240
Oh!

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.210
Using the dead to make a profit...

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.140
This heap of junk...

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.960
You mustn't, Jirou-sama!

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.220
Shinjuurou!

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.760
Jirou-sama?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.600
Ootsubo, what is this?

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.740
They've been murdered... huh.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:00.370
This has become quite interesting.

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:03.490
Because it involves Shimada Hakurou-shi?

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:06.030
I don't care about Shimada-san.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:08.000
I'm talking about the Defeated Detective.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.130
The two dead that were found were both former Rising Sun Association members.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.400
Mitsuhisa! Gomi!

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:15.640
They were recently in the service of Yamamoto Sadanobu's opposing political association.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:20.980
How mysterious. Why on Earth were they both killed, then put inside the statue?

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.390
It's a Trojan horse.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:24.270
Why were they inside that thing?

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.640
Those men were subordinates of yours, weren't they?

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.940
What are you planning?

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:32.990
Wait a second! That statue had no need for an access panel.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:37.160
That means that the only person who could be aware of it is its creator.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.290
Y-You killed those two?

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.210
Your men are weak enough to be killed by a girl like this?

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:47.430
What did you say, you bastard?!

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:48.900
How dare you insult my men!

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.170
It wasn't Youko, father!

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.680
I was the one who requested Youko to do it.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.830
I asked her to hide those two within the statue,

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.940
in order to smuggle them inside the memorial hall.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.480
I believe Yamamoto-san is aware of this as well.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:09.730
The two were ordered by Yamamoto to find the gold bars hidden somewhere in the memorial hall.

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.610
Ah, the rumoured gold bars.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.070
I see. In the newly built memorial hall, it
would be possible to hide them anywhere.

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.490
But why did Jirou do such a thing?

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:23.450
Shimada Jirou was opposed to the way
that his father was publicising himself...

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:26.000
...by using the story of those three men throwing their lives away.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:30.010
Both Gomi-san and Mitsuhisa-san knew how I felt.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:35.260
That's why they cooperated with me in my plan to seize the gold bars and bring them before the public.

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.390
I then requested Youko's assistance in forming a Trojan horse style plan.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:44.680
Last night, at my studio, the two entered the statue...

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:46.900
...at which point the statue was transported here.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.150
I'm responsible for this entire situation.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.330
Jirou... Dammit! You actually believed them about the gold ba-

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.760
For now, I need you to give me all the details.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.280
It's not the time for that.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.790
You said the victims were carried along inside the statue?

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:01.860
What happened then?

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:06.570
The question is who killed them.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.920
The plan was for them to emerge
from the statue before the sun rose,

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.070
and search out the location of the gold bars.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:17.560
But the two of them were murdered and stuffed back into the statue.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.420
Last night, there were perhaps a few of
Ootsubo's men within the hall's grounds.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:25.430
But they were stationed at the front gate and were not alone at any given time.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:29.270
But there was still one other person there, correct? Shimada Hakurou.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:34.280
You're saying that I killed Mitsuhisa and Gomi?!

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.780
You were here alone last evening.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.160
You discovered the two of them emerging from the statue,

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.040
and murdered them in order to protect the gold bars.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:47.040
Unsure what to do with the bodies, you returned them to the statue.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.540
There's no way that cou-

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.390
I believe you're capable of it,

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.550
having killed those three young men without hesitation.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:55.020
What do you mean by that?

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.300
The story is famous.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.300
I'm talking about that terrorist attack.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:03.680
This man forced those three to drive that truck away from the area,

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.690
For the sole purpose of creating a sense of obligation among his supporters.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:09.190
But the truck blew up sooner than expected.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:11.180
You bastard! Do you have proof of that?

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:12.400
No.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:17.470
Even if that terrorist bombing was all an act, there's no proof.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.970
Are you saying that I killed Suzuki and the others through terrorist acts?!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.410
Nothing is certain.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:28.790
But if you've killed even more people now, simply for the purpose of protecting the money you attained by elevating their heroic deeds...

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.290
...I'll never forgive you.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.420
Y-You again?!

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.510
This individual is my boss, basically.

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:44.410
You seem quite worked up.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:48.020
I'm aware that only pitiless deaths exist on the battlefield.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.170
There are no heroic tales...

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.520
...nor are there heroes.

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:57.530
People have no choice...

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.870
...but to answer her question.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:07.870
I expect that you were worried as to whether
those two would be able to find the gold bars.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:11.150
Come now, <i>I'll</i> ask him

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:15.790
Shimada Jirou, you returned here last night, did you not?

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.050
What did you see here?

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.640
Tell me...

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.310
You think that he witnessed it...?

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:27.290
...Shimada-shi killing the two of them?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.680
We'll know soon.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:29.810
What...

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.690
...did you see?

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:39.440
I... returned here while it was still dark,

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:43.460
telling Ootsubo and his men that I was concerned about the statue.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:45.070
But.. we didn't find anything alarming.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.080
What did you see?

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:48.830
Father was...

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.450
Shimada Hakurou was...

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.960
...sleeping. Just as we had planned.

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:03.340
I had put a sleeping drug in father's favourite tea,

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.230
enough so that he wouldn't wake until morning.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:09.100
The plan was to find the gold bars before then.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.880
You said he was sleeping?!

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.730
That's what I was trying to tell all of you!

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.360
Therefore, there's no way I <i>could</i> have killed them!

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:19.330
This is a testimony from his son... Could it be that he's covering for his father?

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:20.790
If we simply analyse the remains of his tea-

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:24.520
Humans cannot lie in response to Inga's question.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:27.870
Shimada Hakurou did not kill those two.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.130
Then who did?!

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:31.730
Who killed them, Defeated Detective?!

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.230
It's unlike Yuuki Shinjuurou to jump so
quickly to a conclusion, wouldn't you say?

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:42.340
And furthermore, for him to declare someone's
innocence upon a confession he himself drew out...

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.870
But with all we know now, who could be the real killer?

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:47.710
How about if I said, "friendly fire"?

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:48.350
Huh?

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:51.350
The two victims killed each other!

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.930
Perhaps they were arguing about how to divide the payment.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.100
By the time they had been transported to the memorial hall grounds,

00:12:57.100 --> 00:13:00.360
they had both likely ceased breathing... Still within the statue.

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:03.680
With this theory, Shimada-san doesn't have to get hurt either.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.120
Is that all right with you?

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:09.370
I wonder if Shimada-san will calm down a bit following this incident.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.200
That idiot!

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:17.960
Hey, Shinjuurou...

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:21.710
Buy me ice cream! Ice cream!

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.420
That soul wasn't nearly enough for me!

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:25.590
Shut up!

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.720
"There are no heroic tales on the battlefield"...

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:31.600
Is that why you think I killed them?

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:36.290
You either threatened them into it, or planned the whole thing yourself.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:39.100
Ah... so, let us assume that it's true.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:43.730
But they died... in the process of saving many.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:46.360
What else is necessary?

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.870
In actuality, they may have been terrified of death,

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:54.240
screaming the names of their lovers, and pissing their pants...

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:58.050
...but did any of them remove the driver's foot from the pedal?

00:13:58.050 --> 00:14:01.780
Everyone wants to live. That is only natural.

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:06.760
Nonetheless, at that moment, they chose to save everyone there.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.380
If they were considering running away, they could have.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.020
But they didn't!

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:15.860
I believe in the selflessness of their intentions,

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:20.020
and wish from the bottom of my heart to
continue passing on their tale of heroism.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:25.350
Young one, you have no understanding of the true beauty of human beings.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.210
According to my father,

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.790
the two of them were victim to "friendly fire".

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.750
What do you think?

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:42.110
It's most certainly another of his lies!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.170
Shimada Hakurou has influence within the military;

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.380
My father is trying to make him indebted to him!

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.430
You're just going to leave it like that?!

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:01.220
You thought that Shimada-san was the culprit from the beginning, didn't you?

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.640
Since he was the kind of person to say things like, "The war was the right thing to do",

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:07.020
and, "Throwing your life away is wonderful"!

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.320
You couldn't forgive him...

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.600
...but you were mistaken.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:13.350
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:17.490
I didn't consider for a second that there could be a culprit other than him.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:20.830
I couldn't even tell him he was wrong.

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:22.210
That he was wrong?

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:28.340
He said that people were able to throw their lives away for the sake of others.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:32.220
I was unable to believe in such things.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:37.640
Human beings live with things in their heart they can't put into words.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:41.480
I assumed that my role was to bring those things to light...

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:44.200
...but I was wrong.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:48.860
You really are the Defeated Detective, aren't you... Yuuki Shinjuurou

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:52.060
I expected so much from you...

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:55.240
This invisible wall that we can always feel surrounding us...

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:58.290
...I thought that you might be able to break through it or something.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.250
Don't go selfishly expecting things from me!

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.150
I know myself!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:08.230
I'm a fool, I'm powerless... And I can't do things for other people...

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.850
...I can't do anything!

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:19.010
Shinjuurou, what's wrong with you?

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:21.490
I'm sure you're not thinking of resigning from being a detective!

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:25.350
After all, you did promise to feed me tons of souls!

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:28.690
Shinjuurou...

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.690
Quite the odd conversation.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:35.220
Humans are just so strange.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.830
Does that mean we're even beyond the
understanding of a worldwide data collective?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:43.030
You thought that Shimada's heroic tale was all a hoax.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.240
But it was the truth.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.290
The truth never changes...

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.650
...it just sullies the beauty of things.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.300
Why are you with Inga?

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.310
So that he can give me souls!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:57.980
Inga!

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.710
Without killing anyone, that is.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:02.430
I was asking about how you first met.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.980
I'm me.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:07.370
It seems you made a deal with Inga:

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:11.490
In exchange for not killing anyone, you would feed him people's souls... Their truths.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:16.280
But you're subsequently aware that this means being possessed by him.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.410
What about it?!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:24.250
Isn't that in itself throwing your life away for the sake of another?

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.630
I'm not that great of a person...

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.170
From my perspective, it's about the same thing.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.000
Shall I tell it to you in percentages?

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.100
The real culprit?

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.350
So they didn't just kill each other?

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.690
It was actually quite simple.

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:52.960
If only my eyes hadn't been following an illusion...

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:57.490
That would be the illusion that someone had sneaked in to steal the gold bars.

00:17:57.490 --> 00:17:58.860
But that's a fact.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:03.740
Before the statue was transported... before they had even entered the statue, the two of them were killed.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.120
And the only person who could have managed that...

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:07.990
...is you.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.910
Why would I do such a thing?

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:13.070
T-That's right! She had no motive!

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.010
As I said, it's simple.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:16.760
Her motive was the gold bars.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.460
Stop joking around!

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:22.800
During yesterday's party, you were the only person inside the building.

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.510
I was tired!

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:28.630
Even with all the commotion happening outside, you didn't leave the building...

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:32.150
...not even after two dead bodies came out of the statue you made?

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:35.070
I didn't want to be... unnecessarily suspected...

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:39.280
From where you were inside, you could clearly see Shimada Hakurou's back.

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:41.860
My back?

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.750
Corpses falling out of a statue.

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:46.260
Anyone with good instincts would suspect a robbery,

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:50.040
and thereafter head for their hidden valuables as quickly as possible.

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:53.820
You were constantly watching for where he might head to.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.000
But he didn't move at all.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.720
Youko...

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:00.760
You knew that the gold bars hadn't been stolen yet...

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:03.990
...since you were the one who killed those two.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:05.870
I didn't want the damn gold bars!

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:09.670
I don't believe that those three that died are heroes!

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:14.350
I believe that they were average kids, who went toward their deaths crying, screaming, "I don't want to die"!

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:16.340
That's why I assisted with your plan!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.530
That's the only reason!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.280
I thought so as well.

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:24.240
That wasn't in the design we approved.

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:26.530
I had thought that it was simply a message from the artist.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:28.180
But...

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:31.920
It's human blood.

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:36.040
Once the police analyse it, we'll know if it's the same as one of the victims.

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:40.800
If they'd killed each other within the statue, there's no way their blood could reach that far outside.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:45.640
The two of them were murdered outside the statue... Before it was transported.

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:50.440
In the middle of the next day, the inside of the statue would become extremely hot.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.940
Following that, the time of death would be impossible to calculate.

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:58.440
The tear I saw on the statue was also an illusion.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:02.200
What should we do?

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:03.930
I'll leave it to you.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:08.330
However, having turned out like this,
I can't just let Shimada-san go unharmed.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:13.210
To be deceived by a beautiful woman... what a hopeless detective.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.520
I suppose I should thank you.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:18.960
I only came to sully a thing of beauty.

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:22.090
Are you saying that that woman is beautiful?

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:27.350
Or are you still doubting the beauty of those men throwing their lives away?

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.040
They certainly did die.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.480
But I'm alive... As are you.

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:34.230
What are you trying to say?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:38.090
There are times when people are forced to give their lives up for others.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.920
But that doesn't mean that you or I are admirable.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.240
The ones who are admirable... Who are beautiful...

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:45.820
...are those men who died, and no one else!

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:48.990
The rest of us are petty, foolish, disorderly...

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.530
...grovelling upon the ground and desperately clinging to life.

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:53.370
That's all.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.930
You...

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:58.880
The reason you didn't panic, even after seeing those thieves...

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:00.710
Inga.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:02.920
Geez...

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:19.900
...was because there no reason for you to panic with it right before your eyes.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:37.460
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:45.380
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:53.060
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:57.440
As if we can see right through it,

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:01.400
We follow it along.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:05.360
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:09.360
Like a falling feather.

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:12.490
Looking for, find it,

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:18.830
So we can come closer together.

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:37.350
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:37.350 --> 00:22:41.350
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:41.350 --> 00:22:44.440
Looking for, find it,

00:22:45.400 --> 00:22:49.280
So we can come closer together.

00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:55.080
The next episode is inspired from "Meiji-era Ango Detective Stories"...

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:56.210
Huh? It's not?

00:22:56.210 --> 00:22:58.960
The original work is a short story called "ANGOU"?

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:00.770
The title has a double meaning, both "angou",

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:03.020
which means a code to hide secrets and then, of course, the author's name.

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:05.090
But who cares about that? I'll give it a read.

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:08.650
It's a great story!

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:10.720
I'm crying tears!

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:16.010
I can't believe Shinjurou and I are going to tamper with a wonderful story like this!

00:23:16.010 --> 00:23:19.020
Next time on UN-GO, "Far too Simple of a Code"!

00:23:19.400 --> 00:23:21.020
What a great feeling...
